{
  "id": "merge-sorted-arrays",
  "order": 21,
  "title": "Merge Two Sorted Arrays",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "pattern": "Two pointers",
  "statement": "Given two integer arrays `nums1` and `nums2`, each sorted in non-decreasing order, return one sorted array containing all their elements.",
  "constraints": [
    "0 <= nums1.length, nums2.length <= 200",
    "-10^9 <= values <= 10^9"
  ],
  "function": {
    "name": "mergeSorted",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "nums1",
        "type": "int[]"
      },
      {
        "name": "nums2",
        "type": "int[]"
      }
    ],
    "returns": "int[]"
  },
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(m + n)",
    "space": "O(m + n)"
  },
  "hints": [
    "Concatenating and sorting is O((m+n) log(m+n)). Both inputs are already sorted, so use that.",
    "Keep one pointer in each array; the smaller current element goes next.",
    "Two pointers; append the smaller head each step, then append whatever remains. (In place in nums1, fill from the back.)"
  ],
  "tests": [
    {
      "args": [
        [
          1,
          2,
          3
        ],
        [
          2,
          5,
          6
        ]
      ],
      "expected": [
        1,
        2,
        2,
        3,
        5,
        6
      ],
      "hidden": false,
      "explanation": "[1,2,2,3,5,6]."
    },
    {
      "args": [
        [
          1
        ],
        []
      ],
      "expected": [
        1
      ],
      "hidden": false,
      "explanation": "One side empty."
    },
    {
